    badge: 'Guildwood badge', cityName: 'Guildwood',
    mission: {"name": "The Quest for the Rescued Stones", "intro": "Old stone has a second life in Guildwood: an 1867 cottage, a garden full of carved fragments, a stage built from a bank. Find the four stamp posts. Each one opens a chapter and a clue to the next.", "chapters": [{"title": "The stone cottage", "text": "Your quest starts at a heritage stone cottage built in 1867 for Councillor Jeremiah Annis and his family. Stone that lasts is the thread of this quest.", "clue": "Head east into the trees. The next post waits where a sculpture garden begins, behind a curved wall of carved figures."}, {"title": "The sculpture sanctuary", "text": "Guild Park is a sculpture sanctuary. Architectural fragments from old buildings decorate its gardens, set here by Rosa and Spencer Clark.", "clue": "Look for a curved stage with eight stone columns. They once stood on a bank downtown."}, {"title": "The bank on the stage", "text": "The Clarks built this open-air theatre from pieces of the historic Bank of Toronto building, demolished around 1960.", "clue": "Follow the stroll down to the lake and east to the bluffs. The last post stands near a bench that faces the water."}, {"title": "The edge of the bluffs", "text": "", "clue": ""}], "finale": "From cottage stone to bank columns to the bluffs themselves, you followed the rescued stones of Guildwood. Mission complete."},
